content.text:
Exactly. The design will prohibit:

- fallback scanners or alternate validation paths;
- nested event/path/label conditionals;
- carry-forward logic that silently substitutes old results;
- duplicated policy in YAML, TOML, and Python;
- exceptions added to keep an oversized gate alive.

The target is one declarative lane decision, one execution path, and one small required result. If a check needs complicated branching to remain mandatory, it should usually be redesigned, moved to advisory, or deleted.
